    "reading": "a corpus dominated by one domain trains a single-domain model whatever its labels say; this is reported so a caller can stage a curriculum or weight the sampler, and is deliberately NOT corrected here"
  },
  "honest_limits": [
    "Promoter-mode corpora are SMALL by construction: yield scales with gene count, not genome size. The corpus size printed here is the real constraint on model size.",
    "One representative per lineage, so within-lineage pangenome content is deliberately not collected -- diversity comes from species, not strains.",
    "The withhold set is computed from the reference genome the falsifier scores on. A future scorer using a different reference or geometry would need its own withhold set, and this corpus would not be gated against it.",
    "Deduplication is exact-sequence. Near-duplicate promoters differing by a base are kept as distinct, so the corpus is an upper bound on truly independent content.",
    "All bacteria, so the domain balance is trivially one-sided; the field exists for the cross-domain phase and is reported rather than corrected."
  ],
